{
  "requirement": "`FileEvidenceStorage::new` retains the root directory without touching the filesystem.\nThe store implements `Send` and `Sync`. Its `load` and `store` futures are `Send`.\n\n`Record`, `Dependency`, and `Fingerprint` support Serde when their type\nparameters do. `Criterion::Ok` is always serializable; its JSON value is\nalready in the record. The SDK supplies `Record<D::NodeData, D::EdgeLabel>` under {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.persisted_dependencies`. Serialization bounds on durable node data and edge labels\napply when using this helper.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `requirements.sdk.filesystem-storage.interface`. All are in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs`.\n\n**`new` retains the root without touching the filesystem**\n- `fn[paths_are_injective_and_loading_missing_records_has_no_side_effects]` builds the store on a nonexistent root. Every `record_path` is asserted equal to `root.join(expected)`, so the root is retained. After many missing-record loads it asserts `!root.exists()`.\n- `fn[send_futures_create_missing_roots_and_nested_paths_without_shortening_keys]` asserts `!root.exists()` right after `new`.\n\n**The store is `Send` and `Sync`**\n- `fn[concurrent_readers_only_observe_complete_records_from_competing_writes]` shares an `Arc<FileEvidenceStorage>` across `std::thread::scope` spawns. That compiles only if the store is `Send` and `Sync`.\n\n**`load` and `store` futures are `Send`**\n- `fn[send_futures_create_missing_roots_and_nested_paths_without_shortening_keys]` passes both the `store` future and the `load` future through `fn send<T: Send>`. This is a compile-time check.\n\n**Serde support for `Record`, `Dependency` and `Fingerprint` when their type parameters do**\n- `fn[records_round_trip_and_malformed_or_incompatible_data_is_an_error]` round-trips records with `Dependency::Node` and `Dependency::OutgoingEdges`. The `Fingerprint` carries a scheme and a value.\n- It also round-trips a record with a `String` edge label. It asserts equal version, dependencies and output after loading.\n- A load with a mismatched label type, `load::<String, u8>`, gives `Json`. So does a load with a mismatched node type, `load::<u8, ()>`.\n- I read `fn[failed_serialization_preserves_records_and_failed_replacement_cleans_up]` from a search snippet only. Its `BadNode` record fails to serialize with `Json`, which shows the bounds apply.\n- The `Dependency` enum has only the two variants above, and both are exercised.\n\n**`Criterion::Ok` is always serializable**\n- This is a trait-bound property: `type Ok: Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send`. The record stores the output as a JSON value, and `fn[records_round_trip_and_malformed_or_incompatible_data_is_an_error]` and the consumer test round-trip that output.\n\n**`Record<D::NodeData, D::EdgeLabel>` under `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.persisted_dependencies`**\n- `fn[consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path]` stores and loads through a domain graph with `String` node data. It asserts the loaded dependencies and output equal the stored ones.\n- The conversion between `NodeId` and node data is the cited requirement's own responsibility. `tests/contracts.rs` already tests it with `fn[saved_node_and_edge_inputs_survive_a_different_handle_allocation_order]`.\n\nI found no gap. The assertions are meaningful and match the requirement text.",
  "references": "4fa7c0209cc8a47ded44aa43c8f5142920833c5dae546977ebf2d7b4b9910690",
